<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6173" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφοτερό-πλοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμφοτερό-πλους</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ουν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>navigable on both sides,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					9.18
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀργύριον</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάνειον</span>) <i>money lent on bottomry,</i> when the
			lender bore the risk <i>of the outward and homeward voyage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐδάνεισα Φορμίωνι κ᾽ μνᾶς
					ἀμφοτερόπλουν εἰς τὸν Πόντον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					34.6
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κέρδος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερόπλουν,</span>
		q.v.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
